    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1024">

                <pb facs="1036" n="916" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg916"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        O’Brien.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee advises Mr. O’Brien that in compliance with the request of the British
                    ambassador he is authorized to use his unofficial friendly offices in support of
                    the British minister’s request for the release of the captain of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Agnes G. Donahoe</hi> on the ground of ill health and
                    because having been in prison already nine months of the ten of his sentence.
                    Mr. O’Brien is advised, however, not to touch the legal merits of the case.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
